<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Mainland Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Kampuchea (1945)</h1><p class="st-meta">1945 CE – 1945 CE · capital Phnom Penh</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Cambodia's first brief independence, declared by King Norodom Sihanouk under Japanese sponsorship in March 1945.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Following the Japanese coup against French rule in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indochina">Indochina</a> on 9 March 1945, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norodom-sihanouk">King Norodom Sihanouk</a> on 13 March annulled the treaties with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and proclaimed the independence of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-cambodia-1953-1970">Cambodia</a>, renamed <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-cambodia">Kampuchea</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmer-empire">Khmer</a> name for the country.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The new government abolished the French romanised script for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmer-empire">Khmer</a> that had been introduced in 1943 and restored the Buddhist lunar calendar. In August 1945 the nationalist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/son-ngoc-thanh">Son Ngoc Thanh</a>, returning from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, became prime minister after a palace coup by his supporters and tried to resist the return of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan's</a> surrender, British and French forces arrived, and in October 1945 the French arrested <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/son-ngoc-thanh">Son Ngoc Thanh</a> and exiled him to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-cambodia-1953-1970">Cambodia</a> returned to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/french-protectorate-of-cambodia">French protectorate of Cambodia</a> as an autonomous kingdom within the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/french-fourth-republic">French Union</a>, regaining full independence in 1953.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-kampuchea-1945.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Kampuchea (1945)" width="320" height="206"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Cambodia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1945 CE – 1945 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Phnom Penh</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Norodom Sihanouk, Son Ngoc Thanh</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Theravada Buddhism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Khmer</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/cambodia">Cambodia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of Kampuchea</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1945&amp;focus=kingdom-of-kampuchea-1945" aria-label="Kingdom of Kampuchea (1945) on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7566 1746 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Kampuchea (1945) lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7886 2002L7886 2002M7886 2002L8529 1145"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7886 2002h0M8529 1145h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7886 2002h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7886 2002h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Phnom Penh. <a href="/atlas?year=1945&amp;focus=kingdom-of-kampuchea-1945">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
